# Frozen vector bytes must never be EOL-normalized. Every file under v1/ is
# pinned by SHA256SUMS, so any autocrlf newline conversion on checkout (e.g. a
# Windows contributor with core.autocrlf=true) would change the bytes and make
# `shasum -a 256 -c SHA256SUMS` fail — for the checkout-er, not the author.
# In-repo attributes override local git config, so the published bytes are the
# bytes everyone gets. Covers the PEM keys, expected.json, and SHA256SUMS too,
# not only the .cose/.bin payloads.
* -text
*.cose binary
*.bin  binary
